From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:58:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sceNpTrophy: ps3_trophy_ready, the set read and the store
 loaded

ps3_trophy_count is nonzero from CreateContext, when the TRP is read, but
the player's unlocks are loaded only at RegisterContext. In Killzone HD the
two are three guest calls apart at boot; a host that read the store between
them saw every trophy locked. Port side: the RecompLauncher bridge lists the
trophies the player already has as "earlier" once, when it connects, and in
a headless boot it connected in that window.

ps3_trophy_ready() is 1 once the title's context has its TRP and is
registered (its store loaded), under the store lock.
---
 libs/network/sceNpTrophy.c | 9 +++++++++
 libs/network/sceNpTrophy.h | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/network/sceNpTrophy.c b/libs/network/sceNpTrophy.c
index c38ea60..4c55009 100644
--- a/libs/network/sceNpTrophy.c
+++ b/libs/network/sceNpTrophy.c
@@ -453,6 +453,15 @@ static TrophyContext* trophy_host_ctx(void)
     return NULL;
 }
 
+int ps3_trophy_ready(void)
+{
+    STORE_LOCK();
+    const TrophyContext* ctx = trophy_host_ctx();
+    const int r = ctx && ctx->have_trp && ctx->registered;
+    STORE_UNLOCK();
+    return r;
+}
+
 int ps3_trophy_count(void)
 {
     STORE_LOCK();
diff --git a/libs/network/sceNpTrophy.h b/libs/network/sceNpTrophy.h
index 587000c..6f45692 100644
--- a/libs/network/sceNpTrophy.h
+++ b/libs/network/sceNpTrophy.h
@@ -207,6 +207,9 @@ typedef struct ps3_trophy_def {
     char name_en[SCE_NP_TROPHY_NAME_MAX_SIZE];   /* TROP.SFM's, as the store keeps it */
 } ps3_trophy_def;
 int ps3_trophy_count(void);
+/* 1 once the set is read and the store loaded (RegisterContext): from then on
+ * ps3_trophy_get's unlocked fields are the player's, not all zero. */
+int ps3_trophy_ready(void);
 int ps3_trophy_get(s32 id, ps3_trophy_def* out);
 
 /* The PNG of trophy `id` (TROPnnn.PNG; -1 = the set's ICON0.PNG), read from
